      "task_outcome_detailed": "TITLE/ABSTRACT SCREENING RESULTS FOR SYSTEMATIC REVIEW: 'Psychological therapies for    
  the treatment of anxiety disorders in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease'. SUMMARY: Total studies screened: 58,    
  Studies INCLUDED: 1 (Study #42), Studies EXCLUDED: 57. SELECTION CRITERIA APPLIED: 1) Study design: RCTs,             
  cluster-randomised trials, or cross-over trials ONLY; 2) Population: People aged >40 years with COPD AND coexisting   
  anxiety disorders (confirmed by diagnostic criteria or validated scale); 3) Intervention: Psychological therapies;    
  4) Comparison: No intervention OR education only; 5) Co-intervention rule: If psychological therapy delivered with    
  another intervention, comparison group must receive co-intervention alone. INCLUDED STUDY (#42): 'COPD education and  
  cognitive behavioral therapy group treatment for clinically significant symptoms of depression and anxiety in COPD    
  patients: a randomised controlled trial' - RCT of CBT vs COPD education in COPD patients with moderate-to-severe      
  anxiety/depression confirmed by validated scales (BAI, BDI-II). EXCLUSION BREAKDOWN: Not RCTs (reviews,               
  cross-sectional, cohort, qualitative, protocols): 36 studies; Wrong population (no confirmed anxiety disorders, not   
  specifically COPD): 12 studies; Wrong intervention (not psychological therapy): 4 studies; Wrong comparison (not      
  education/no intervention): 5 studies; Co-intervention without proper control: 1 study; Other reasons: 1 study.",     
      "additional_context": "SCREENING NOTES: 1) Conservative approach applied - when uncertain about anxiety disorder  
  confirmation, studies were excluded as criteria require confirmed anxiety disorders. 2) Many RCTs excluded because    
  they studied COPD patients generally rather than those with confirmed anxiety disorders. 3) Several studies combined  
  psychological interventions with other treatments but lacked appropriate control groups. 4) Only Study 42 clearly     
  met all criteria: recruited COPD patients with moderate-to-severe anxiety symptoms confirmed by validated scales,     
  used CBT, compared to COPD education only. 5) Low inclusion rate (1/58) reflects specificity of criteria requiring    
  both confirmed anxiety disorders AND appropriate control conditions. RECOMMENDATIONS: Verify Study 42's age           
  criterion (>40 years), confirm exact nature of 'COPD education' control, check borderline exclusions for full-text    
  review."                                                                                                              
  })                                                                                                                    
